{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"ananse-and-the-pot-of-wisdom","version":1,"title":"Ananse and the Pot of Wisdom","ageTiers":["5-6","7-8"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"Long ago, Ananse the spider decided that he would be the wisest creature in the world. ‘If I keep all the wisdom for myself,’ he thought, ‘everyone will have to ask me for help.’","sentences":["Long ago, Ananse the spider decided that he would be the wisest creature in the world.","‘If I keep all the wisdom for myself,’ he thought, ‘everyone will have to ask me for help.’"],"image":"sha256:48e03081aeaed7fde6d8a4d78efb57ca5ac2773ccd70d23c2f4a3782982311d7","alt":"A proud spider in a small cap stands tall in a village square.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:c62185d3c1f495bcff963f77d5afe051d8667bbc3f2f0034b42a88ca2323ea4a","durationMs":14560,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,7321],[7321,14560]],"words":[[0,345],[345,1034],[1034,1551],[1551,1809],[1809,2326],[2326,2929],[2929,3274],[3274,3446],[3446,3877],[3877,4049],[4049,4307],[4307,4824],[4824,5513],[5513,5685],[5685,5943],[5943,7321],[7321,7493],[7493,7665],[7665,8010],[8010,8268],[8268,8526],[8526,9043],[9043,9301],[9301,10249],[10249,10421],[10421,11455],[11455,12144],[12144,12489],[12489,12834],[12834,13006],[13006,13264],[13264,13436],[13436,13694],[13694,14560]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"For many days Ananse went from village to village. He gathered wise sayings, clever ideas and good advice. He put them all into a big clay pot.","sentences":["For many days Ananse went from village to village.","He gathered wise sayings, clever ideas and good advice.","He put them all into a big clay pot."],"image":"sha256:bc5a8f758541459c239c13c5aa65322a7842ed43ce732e96c8b3e580c59ed1ca","alt":"The spider collects glowing ideas into a large clay pot in a market.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:b8ee17c3c89502e6180c72f4b5d8494081ae73dd1d01c99e36eb3b377e9995f9","durationMs":14000,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4952],[4952,10761],[10761,14000]],"words":[[0,286],[286,667],[667,1048],[1048,1619],[1619,2000],[2000,2381],[2381,3048],[3048,3238],[3238,4952],[4952,5142],[5142,5904],[5904,6285],[6285,7428],[7428,7999],[7999,8475],[8475,8761],[8761,9142],[9142,10761],[10761,10951],[10951,11237],[11237,11618],[11618,11904],[11904,12285],[12285,12475],[12475,12761],[12761,13142],[13142,14000]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"When the pot was full, Ananse carried it into the forest. ‘I will hide this at the top of the tallest tree,’ he said, ‘where nobody can ever reach it.’","sentences":["When the pot was full, Ananse carried it into the forest.","‘I will hide this at the top of the tallest tree,’ he said, ‘where nobody can ever reach it.’"],"image":"sha256:1418c42080e05bcd122036924f051326b8aec79e2834b42cd6ab78ddfef22dc3","alt":"The spider stands at the foot of a very tall tree holding the pot.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:0631b3a53932e140c564c30bbfc414449ad0a34806c3e89542aebf46908f7b00","durationMs":13920,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5815],[5815,13920]],"words":[[0,381],[381,667],[667,953],[953,1239],[1239,2097],[2097,2669],[2669,3336],[3336,3527],[3527,3908],[3908,4194],[4194,5815],[5815,6006],[6006,6387],[6387,6768],[6768,7149],[7149,7340],[7340,7626],[7626,7912],[7912,8103],[8103,8389],[8389,9056],[9056,9914],[9914,10105],[10105,10963],[10963,11440],[11440,12012],[12012,12298],[12298,12679],[12679,13156],[13156,13920]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"Ananse tied the pot to his tummy and began to climb. But the pot kept bumping against the trunk. He slid down. He tried again. Bump! He slid down again.","sentences":["Ananse tied the pot to his tummy and began to climb.","But the pot kept bumping against the trunk.","He slid down.","He tried again.","Bump!","He slid down again."],"image":"sha256:16ee8ebd80ba8a18c553decb12d4f5ee0305a48bdcdd26a772f507c5a4c0670f","alt":"The spider slips down the tree trunk with a big pot tied in front of him.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:1a50cb143733e1bd9a7ed8a0e1476b0833d4015ef988d7c0525329716544f963","durationMs":13080,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3819],[3819,7197],[7197,8740],[8740,10430],[10430,11532],[11532,13080]],"words":[[0,441],[441,735],[735,955],[955,1175],[1175,1322],[1322,1542],[1542,1909],[1909,2129],[2129,2496],[2496,2643],[2643,3819],[3819,4039],[4039,4259],[4259,4479],[4479,4773],[4773,5287],[5287,5801],[5801,6021],[6021,7197],[7197,7344],[7344,7638],[7638,8740],[8740,8887],[8887,9254],[9254,10430],[10430,11532],[11532,11679],[11679,11973],[11973,12267],[12267,13080]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"His young son Ntikuma had followed him quietly. ‘Papa,’ he said, ‘why not tie the pot on your back? Then your arms and legs are free to climb.’","sentences":["His young son Ntikuma had followed him quietly.","‘Papa,’ he said, ‘why not tie the pot on your back?","Then your arms and legs are free to climb.’"],"image":"sha256:fb1344d107d5f3d95336588edb2576e2f870758649961a7b7f527151b2ee2d37","alt":"A small spider points to his father’s back while the father looks surprised.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:1b961d3d7ced55811f414acaaea461b272c5ee8f0f1d7ffbddc462b589958184","durationMs":11680,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4029],[4029,8541],[8541,11680]],"words":[[0,242],[242,645],[645,887],[887,1451],[1451,1693],[1693,2337],[2337,2579],[2579,4029],[4029,4754],[4754,4915],[4915,5640],[5640,5882],[5882,6124],[6124,6366],[6366,6608],[6608,6850],[6850,7011],[7011,7333],[7333,8541],[8541,8863],[8863,9185],[9185,9507],[9507,9749],[9749,10071],[10071,10313],[10313,10635],[10635,10796],[10796,11680]]}}},{"n":6,"text":"Ananse stopped. He was shocked. ‘I thought I had gathered all the wisdom,’ he said, ‘yet my small son has an idea that I did not have!’","sentences":["Ananse stopped.","He was shocked.","‘I thought I had gathered all the wisdom,’ he said, ‘yet my small son has an idea that I did not have!’"],"image":"sha256:a2c5126b553fa3054351b38d8ff66208e59b729a3e87a244342bf92f95936089","alt":"The spider stares at his son with wide eyes beside the tall tree.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:4566ee43c57be196f84595c0f2069cb289110e3e82c6979ca10af302b08e44a6","durationMs":11520,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,1961],[1961,3840],[3840,11520]],"words":[[0,490],[490,1961],[1961,2124],[2124,2369],[2369,3840],[3840,4003],[4003,4575],[4575,4738],[4738,4983],[4983,5637],[5637,5882],[5882,6127],[6127,7026],[7026,7189],[7189,7924],[7924,8169],[8169,8332],[8332,8741],[8741,8986],[8986,9231],[9231,9394],[9394,9721],[9721,10048],[10048,10211],[10211,10456],[10456,10701],[10701,11520]]}}},{"n":7,"text":"Ananse was so cross that he threw the pot to the ground. It broke, and the wisdom flew out in every direction. People across the land found a little of it.","sentences":["Ananse was so cross that he threw the pot to the ground.","It broke, and the wisdom flew out in every direction.","People across the land found a little of it."],"image":"sha256:ad5648ffeab0ea7dd9708f8bd99510739eef775a127e0cf41d951aed5d30aff9","alt":"A clay pot shatters and glowing ideas float across hills and villages.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:8252584502e8edebd6240191dba17e9e72ac9a23f145ef2fcccb274efa27dce1","durationMs":14840,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5264],[5264,10815],[10815,14840]],"words":[[0,574],[574,861],[861,1052],[1052,1531],[1531,1914],[1914,2105],[2105,2584],[2584,2871],[2871,3158],[3158,3349],[3349,3636],[3636,5264],[5264,5455],[5455,6412],[6412,6699],[6699,6986],[6986,7560],[7560,7943],[7943,8230],[8230,8421],[8421,8900],[8900,10815],[10815,11389],[11389,11963],[11963,12250],[12250,12633],[12633,13112],[13112,13303],[13303,13877],[13877,14068],[14068,14840]]}}},{"n":8,"text":"That is why nobody has all the wisdom, and why even a child can share a good idea. Ananse learned to listen. The end.","sentences":["That is why nobody has all the wisdom, and why even a child can share a good idea.","Ananse learned to listen.","The end."],"image":"sha256:a45e057949b73424cb5106d7922c1b993bddb781dd93020f13d54b674dfeeed0","alt":"The spider sits with his son under the tree, listening, as people in the distance share ideas.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:91924407d4f910448da7c1cb497a79ea7413883ef55e7543b83c97a6bb655ee8","durationMs":11600,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,7515],[7515,10486],[10486,11600]],"words":[[0,371],[371,557],[557,835],[835,1392],[1392,1670],[1670,1948],[1948,2226],[2226,3247],[3247,3525],[3525,3803],[3803,4174],[4174,4360],[4360,4824],[4824,5102],[5102,5566],[5566,5752],[5752,6123],[6123,7515],[7515,8072],[8072,8722],[8722,8908],[8908,10486],[10486,10764],[10764,11600]]}}}],"activities":[{"id":"wisdom-c1","type":"comprehension","afterPage":2,"question":"Why did Ananse want to keep all the wisdom?","options":["So everyone would have to ask him for help","So he could give it away","So he could sell it"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"wisdom-voc","type":"vocabulary","afterPage":1,"word":"wisdom","definition":"Good understanding and sensible ideas.","distractors":["A kind of food","A tall tree"]},{"id":"wisdom-c2","type":"comprehension","afterPage":5,"question":"What was Ntikuma’s idea?","options":["Tie the pot on his back","Carry the pot in his mouth","Leave the pot at home"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"wisdom-p1","type":"prediction","afterPage":6,"prompt":"Ananse has been shown a better idea by his own son. What will he do?","options":["Say thank you and listen","Get angry","Hide the pot somewhere else"]},{"id":"wisdom-s1","type":"sequencing","afterPage":8,"prompt":"Put the story in order.","items":["Ananse gathered wisdom into a pot.","Ntikuma suggested tying the pot on his back.","The pot broke and wisdom spread everywhere.","Ananse learned to listen."]},{"id":"wisdom-sel","type":"sel","afterPage":8,"prompt":"How might Ananse have felt when his son had the better idea? How do you feel when someone younger helps you?","feelingOptions":["Surprised","Embarrassed","Proud","Grateful"]}],"glossary":[{"word":"creature","definition":"A living animal or being.","pages":[1]},{"word":"advice","definition":"Helpful ideas about what to do.","pages":[2]},{"word":"wisdom","definition":"Good understanding and sensible ideas.","pages":[1,7,8]}],"assets":{"sha256:c62185d3c1f495bcff963f77d5afe051d8667bbc3f2f0034b42a88ca2323ea4a":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/c62185d3c1f4.mp3","bytes":58701,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:48e03081aeaed7fde6d8a4d78efb57ca5ac2773ccd70d23c2f4a3782982311d7":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/ananse-and-the-pot-of-wisdom/page1-1.webp","bytes":87926,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:b8ee17c3c89502e6180c72f4b5d8494081ae73dd1d01c99e36eb3b377e9995f9":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/b8ee17c3c895.mp3","bytes":56493,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:bc5a8f758541459c239c13c5aa65322a7842ed43ce732e96c8b3e580c59ed1ca":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/ananse-and-the-pot-of-wisdom/page2-1.webp","bytes":88970,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:0631b3a53932e140c564c30bbfc414449ad0a34806c3e89542aebf46908f7b00":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/0631b3a53932.mp3","bytes":56109,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:1418c42080e05bcd122036924f051326b8aec79e2834b42cd6ab78ddfef22dc3":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/ananse-and-the-pot-of-wisdom/page3-1.webp","bytes":88706,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:1a50cb143733e1bd9a7ed8a0e1476b0833d4015ef988d7c0525329716544f963":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/1a50cb143733.mp3","bytes":52749,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:16ee8ebd80ba8a18c553decb12d4f5ee0305a48bdcdd26a772f507c5a4c0670f":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/ananse-and-the-pot-of-wisdom/page4-1.webp","bytes":87614,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:1b961d3d7ced55811f414acaaea461b272c5ee8f0f1d7ffbddc462b589958184":{"path":"/story-spark-prev